Perhaps I'm a total idiot, but I don't think you are quite correct;  I
think this is a preference list that will use items in the order listed
-- except wand of death, which is a
last resort.


See, If we encounter the first item higher up the list, we drop through
the loop and  retain the first item.  If the second item is higher, we
will switch to the second item. So if I'm reading this correctly, if we
had a wand of sleep and a wand of
fire, we'd use the wand of sleep first, since it's higher on the list.


However, the check has been disabled for wand of death -- so a wand of
death
is a last resort item. It will be used after everything else.

So if we had a wand of death, sleep, and fire,  the monster would use
sleep, fire,
death.

Judging by the fact that nomore (WAND_DEATH) is commented out, that has

to be a deliberate change.

I can think of three reasons why this would happen:

1) Game balance.  Makes a death from gnome with wand of death less
likely.

2) Saves the wand for the player.  If it's at the top,  the monster
might waste
all the charges and leave the player a (0:0) wand. It happens often
enough anyway.

3) Reserves the charges for the monster.  If you're clever and send an
armada
of pets at him first,  he'll use up his lesser wands and save up the
death ray for YOU.

Otherwise, with a ring of conflict or some such one could trick a
monster into using
up it's wand of death on other creatures, leaving it with weaker wands
to take you on.

